      "source_unit_key": "policy-optimization.html::node-1465",
      "source_sha256": "f6712eb065a78bbca3a62825900e431a7404ad8d0f425c7941f07472f704ad94",
      "unit_text_sha256": "5b41a24988f21dabc99610b29e5c5a784f8a04d27504e697bf5e3c03d59f5372",
      "source_text": "\n            (a) The unconstrained minimiser $\\theta=2$ is infeasible, so the constraint is active: $\\bar\\theta=1$, and stationarity $2(\\bar\\theta-2)+\\bar\\lambda=0$ gives $\\bar\\lambda=2$.\n            (b) For $\\theta\\le1$, $F_\\kappa=(\\theta-2)^2$ is decreasing. For $\\theta\\gt1$, $F_\\kappa'(\\theta)=2(\\theta-2)+\\kappa$ vanishes at $\\theta=2-\\kappa/2$. If $\\kappa\\lt2$ this point lies above 1 and is the minimiser, infeasible by $1-\\kappa/2$ (e.g. $\\kappa=1$: $\\theta=1.5$). If $\\kappa\\ge2$, $F_\\kappa$ is increasing on $\\theta\\gt1$ and $\\bar\\theta=1$ is the unique minimiser. Threshold: $\\kappa\\ge\\bar\\lambda=2$ (at $\\kappa=2$ the minimiser is still unique here because $f$ is strictly convex).\n            (c) Quadratic penalty: for $\\theta\\gt1$, $2(\\theta-2)+\\mu(\\theta-1)=0$ gives $\\theta_\\mu=\\frac{4+\\mu}{2+\\mu}$, infeasible by $\\frac{2}{2+\\mu}$ for every finite $\\mu$ ($\\mu=10$: $0.167$; $\\mu=100$: $0.020$). Barrier: for $\\theta\\lt1$, $2(\\theta-2)+\\frac{1}{t(1-\\theta)}=0$; with $u=1-\\theta$ this is $2u^2+2u=1/t$, so $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+2/t}-1}{2}\\approx\\frac{1}{2t}$. The iterate is strictly feasible and the objective gap is $f(\\theta_t)-f(\\bar\\theta)=(1+u)^2-1=2u+u^2=\\frac1t-u^2\\le\\frac1t$: exactly IPO's $m/t$ bound with $m=1$ ($t=10$: $0.098\\le0.1$). The implied multiplier $\\lambda_t=\\frac{1}{tu}$ equals $2.10$ at $t=10$ and $2.01$ at $t=100$, converging to $\\bar\\lambda=2$: the barrier follows the central path. Only the ReLU penalty is exact at a finite weight, and that weight is the unknown $\\bar\\lambda$; hence P3O's schedule $\\kappa\\leftarrow\\min(\\rho\\kappa,\\kappa_{\\max})$.\n            (d) Minimise $-\\theta$ subject to $\\theta\\le0$: $\\bar\\theta=0$, $\\bar\\lambda=1$. With $\\kappa=1$, $F(\\theta)=-\\theta+\\max\\{0,\\theta\\}=\\max\\{-\\theta,0\\}$ attains its minimum $0$ at every $\\theta\\ge0$, including every infeasible $\\theta\\gt0$; for $\\kappa\\gt1$ the minimiser $\\theta=0$ is unique, for $\\kappa\\lt1$ there is none. This is why part (b) of the theorem in Section 4 needs $\\kappa\\gt\\|\\bar\\lambda\\|_\\infty$.\n          ",
